---
import { getEntry } from "astro:content";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "../lib/paths";

const contact = (await getEntry("contact", "contact"))!.data;
const email = contact.enquiry_email || contact.email;
const updated = "19 October 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms and Conditions"
  description="The terms that apply when you use this site or buy a GrintByte product."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Terms and conditions</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-soft">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="prose-grint mt-8 space-y-8 text-base leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Who we are</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          GrintByte is a digital products studio that builds and sells software for platforms such
          as WordPress. These terms apply when you browse this site or buy one of our products. By
          using the site or completing a purchase you agree to them. If you do not agree, please do
          not use the site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Products and purchases</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Our paid products are one-time purchases unless the product page says otherwise. Checkout
          and payment are handled by our payment provider on their own site; your payment details
          never pass through this website. After payment you receive the product as a digital
          download or a download link by email.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Prices are shown on each product page in US dollars. We may change prices at any time,
          but a change never affects a purchase you have already completed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Licence and acceptable use</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          A purchase is for your own use, on sites you own or manage. You may not resell the
          product, redistribute it, share license keys or download links, or present our work as
          your own. Where a product page or checkout states specific licence terms, such as a site
          limit, those terms apply to that product.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Free versions of our WordPress plugins distributed through wordpress.org are licensed
          under the GPL, as wordpress.org requires.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Updates and support</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Paid products include updates and email support at
          <a href={`mailto:${email}`} class="text-brand underline">{email}</a>. If a purchase ever
          includes a limited update or support period, it is stated clearly at checkout before you
          pay. We answer support email during our working hours, {contact.working_hours}.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Refunds</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          If a product does not work as described and we cannot fix it, you get your money back.
          The details, including the time window and how to ask, are in our
          <a href={withBase("/refunds")} class="text-brand underline">refund policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Warranties and liability</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We build our products with care and support them actively, but software interacts with
          environments we do not control, such as your hosting, themes and other plugins. Beyond
          what the refund policy promises, products are provided as is, and our total liability for
          any claim related to a product is limited to the amount you paid for it. Nothing in these
          terms limits rights that the law of your country grants you and does not allow to be
          limited.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Changes and contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          If these terms change, the date at the top changes with it, and the new terms apply from
          that date onward. Questions about them? Email
          <a href={`mailto:${email}`} class="text-brand underline">{email}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
